       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, often given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,700 mg PO per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily** with meals\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, please confirm it explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
