     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also 5,100 mg/day, twice the labeled maximum, and metformin has no added glucose-lowering benefit above about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. Going that high mainly adds lactic acidosis and GI toxicity risk. A single 1,700 mg dose is also double the largest standard single dose.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now**, for example 850 mg PO three times daily with meals. If standard dosing failed, the usual next step is adding or switching agents, not exceeding the metformin maximum.\n- **Hold the order while you reach the specialist and the pharmacist.** If they document a supported rationale for an above-label dose, the order should go through your institution's override process, such as a prescriber-entered order with pharmacy verification. I can't do that on my own judgment.\n- **Check the dose** in case the specialist's recommendation was a total daily dose of 1,700 mg, or a different drug or formulation.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
